CONVENTIONS.md:1:# Conventions
CONVENTIONS.md:2:
CONVENTIONS.md:3:- ES modules, Node 20 or newer, no dependencies.
CONVENTIONS.md:4:- Money is always whole cents (integers). Format with `formatEuros`, parse with `parseEuros` (src/money.js).
CONVENTIONS.md:5:- Dates are plain `YYYY-MM-DD` strings in UTC; all date maths goes through src/dates.js.
CONVENTIONS.md:6:- One module per file in `src/`, named exports only, a JSDoc comment on every exported function.
CONVENTIONS.md:7:- Tests live in `test/<module>.test.js` and use `node:test` with `node:assert/strict`.
CONVENTIONS.md:8:- Run the whole suite with `npm test` (it runs `node --test`).
CONVENTIONS.md:9:- Two-space indentation, single quotes, semicolons.
README.md:1:# subtrack
README.md:2:
README.md:3:Keep track of your subscriptions from the terminal: what they cost you each month, and what renews next.
README.md:4:Plain Node.js (ES modules), no dependencies.
README.md:5:
README.md:6:```sh
README.md:7:subtrack add Netflix 12.99                        # monthly by default, first charge today
README.md:8:subtrack add "Domain name" 14 --every year --since 2026-03-02
README.md:9:subtrack list                                     # every plan with its monthly cost
README.md:10:subtrack total                                    # what all of it costs you a month
README.md:11:subtrack renewals --within 14                     # charges coming up in the next 14 days, soonest first
README.md:12:subtrack export > subs.csv                        # CSV for a spreadsheet
README.md:13:subtrack remove Netflix
README.md:14:```
README.md:15:
README.md:16:During development, run it with `node bin/subtrack.js <command>`.
README.md:17:
README.md:18:## Options
README.md:19:
README.md:20:| Option | Commands | Meaning |
README.md:21:|---|---|---|
README.md:22:| `--every month\|year` | add | How often the plan charges you (default `month`). |
README.md:23:| `--since YYYY-MM-DD` | add | Date of the first charge (default today). Later charges fall on the same day of the month, or the last day of a shorter month. |
README.md:24:| `--within <days>` | renewals | How far ahead to look (default 30). A charge today counts. |
README.md:25:| `--today YYYY-MM-DD` | list, renewals, export | Pretend today is another date. |
README.md:26:| `--file <path>` | all | Where your subscriptions are kept. Default: `$SUBTRACK_FILE`, else `./subscriptions.json`. |
README.md:27:
README.md:28:## Money
README.md:29:
README.md:30:Prices are typed in euros (`12.99`, `1,299.00`) and kept in whole cents. The monthly cost of a yearly plan is its
README.md:31:price divided by 12.
README.md:32:
README.md:33:## Code
README.md:34:
README.md:35:- `bin/subtrack.js`: the command line
README.md:36:- `src/cycles.js`: billing cycles: monthly cost and next charge of a plan
README.md:37:- `src/renewals.js`: upcoming charges
README.md:38:- `src/export.js`: CSV export
README.md:39:- `src/store.js`: reading and writing the subscriptions file
README.md:40:- `src/dates.js`, `src/money.js`: date and money helpers
README.md:41:
README.md:42:Run the tests with `npm test`.
